      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">افغرهُ عَلَيْهِ</span></b> ; (ISk, S, O, K;) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فخّرهُ</span></b> 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عليه</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفْخِيرٌ</span>; (ISk, S, O;) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عليه</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَخَرَهُ</span></b> ,
aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَخَرَ</span></b> , (AZ, O, * K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَخْرٌ</span>; (AZ, O, TA;)
<i>He judged him,</i> or <i>made him, to excel,</i> or <i>to have
excelled, him in</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَخْر</span> [or <i>glorying,</i> or <i>boasting,</i> or
<i>glory,</i> or <i>excellence</i>]. (ISk, S, O, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفْخَرَتْ</span>
<i>She</i> (a woman) <i>brought forth none but such as
was</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَاخِر</span> [or <i>goodly,</i> &amp;c.]. (Lth, O.)

